The compute units on which a GPU's processes run (runtime/compute-units.cpp,
docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU processes that run loops, one kernel for a GPU's
processes): the pairs of those its queues may use, units 2P and 2P + 1, as
LIBOMPTARGET_AMDGPU_CU_MASK leaves them, of which the processes' kernel takes
the lowest pairs, a percentage of them rounded up (MERK_GPU_PROCESS_UNITS,
process.set_gpu_units), here 50% and 1%. The mask is the host's, so the test
needs no GPU.

RUN: clang++ -O2 -std=c++17 %S/Inputs/compute-units-test.cpp %S/../../runtime/compute-units.cpp -o %t
RUN: %t | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines

CHECK: 80 units: 0000ffff ffffffff ffffffff (80), 50% 00000000 000000ff ffffffff, 1% 00000000 00000000 00000003
CHECK-NEXT: units 0-39: 00000000 000000ff ffffffff (40), 50% 00000000 00000000 000fffff, 1% 00000000 00000000 00000003

Units 1 and 6 have no pair, so they are not used.
CHECK-NEXT: units 1-6: 00000000 00000000 0000003c (4), 50% 00000000 00000000 0000000c, 1% 00000000 00000000 0000000c
CHECK-NEXT: units 0, 2 and 4: none
CHECK-NEXT: a unit beyond the 256th: none
